# ---- JOB OUTPUT: 1.5 GB of it, and it lives HERE now ----
# `results/` was at `~/artifacts/TRD-EHR/results/` and it was moved into this
# workspace on 14 September 2026, deliberately, so that a project's output sits
# with the project. It is regenerable -- every file in it is written by a job
# in `slurm_jobs/` -- and seven of them are over GitHub's 50 MB warning, so it
# stays out of git. The rule was already here; what is new is that there is now
# something on the other side of it. `board/test/tracked.py` fails the suite if
# any of it is ever tracked.
artifacts/
__pycache__/
test_data/
logs/
scratch/
.DS_Store
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*cancel*.sh
endpoints/
results/
.claude/
.vscode/
figures/
node_modules/
writeup/
slurm-*.out

# live tutoring board (Tutor-Board) — scratch space, never tracked
live/

# ---- Other authors' published papers: on disk, never tracked ----
# This repository is public. The two citation libraries hold published PDFs
# whose copyright belongs to their authors and publishers, so they live here
# for reading and stay out of git. Everything WE wrote is tracked: the
# manuscript, supplement, TRIPOD+AI checklist, cover letter, the reserve and
# review documents, the library indexes (README.md, CITATION_MAP.md), the
# role-grouped manifests, the reprint-request drafts, and the SFHS data
# provenance note. A clone therefore arrives with the bibliography described
# but not carried; CITATION_MAP.md says what each missing prefix is.
paper1-trd-prediction/references/*.pdf
paper2-counterfactual/references/*.pdf
paper2-counterfactual/references/*_SUPPL-APPENDIX.docx
paper2-counterfactual/references/*_METHODS-SUPPLEMENT.docx

# The TRIPOD+AI reporting guideline is Collins et al. 2024 (BMJ) -- someone
# else's paper. The JMIR submission template is ours to use and is tracked.
formats/TripodAI.pdf

# ---- this machine's own configuration ----
# `.env` names the on-disk locations of identifiable patient data on lab
# storage: the person-level CSVs, the patient JSON directory, the cohort file.
# It was tracked for 477 commits and it has been removed from all of them,
# because a public repository that publishes a map to where the PHI is kept has
# published something about the PHI. `.env.example` carries the KEYS, so a
# clone knows what to fill in and learns nothing about this machine.
.env
